  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5134",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 appears to interact with LS-513 through a series of molecular pathways involving the enzyme 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The drug is predicted to target multiple entities, including Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, TE-11, and GCIY, all of which are targets of the same compound. This suggests that palmarumycin CP18 may exert its effects by modulating the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn influences LS-513. The shared target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid across multiple targets of palmarumycin CP18 implies a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of this compound's activity. The evidence supports a pathway where palmarumycin CP18 indirectly affects LS-513 through the modulation of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, highlighting a possible role in metabolic or signaling pathways.",
